                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="368-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ></span>Electro-Voice 635A</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Omnidirectional Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The EV635 is a rugged, compact omnidirectional dynamic microphone popular in the news industry. </p><p>According to EV:</p><ul><li>This is the best known news gathering microphone in the world</li><li>It is incredibly durable</li><li>It is known as &#8220;The Buchanan Hammer&#8221; (a nickname appropriated from the discontinued <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Electro-Voice/664">Electro-Voice 664</a>, presumably for marketing reasons)</li></ul><p>Two colors are available:</p><ul><li><b>635A</b> - Fawn Beige</li><li><b>635B</b> - Semi-Gloss black</li></ul><p>Both models have a steel case and a 4-stage pop filter. The mic takes the EV 311 stand adapter, and will fit any 19mm mic clip.</p><p>The 635 enjoys a strong following among rec.audio.pro members:</p><blockquote><p><cite>Scott Dorsey</cite>You should be ashamed of yourself for not owning any EV 635As. They cost less than SM57s and are just as versatile. <a href="http://groups.google.com/group/rec.audio.pro/msg/eaf2d815add849b7?dmode=source">This is like having a studio without a coffee machine</a>.</p></blockquote><p>But note that that quote is from 1998.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s lack of low end and lack of proximity effect make it useful in certain situations such as miking guitar cabinets and some vocals.</p><p>The 635A comes up in conversation often on The Home Recording Show Podcast by host Ryan Canestro. Episode 127 features a shootout with the <a href="http://www.homerecordingshow.com/2011/07/show-127-bass-amp-mic-comparison-and-more/" target="blank">EV 635A on Bass cabinet</a>. </p><p>See also the neodymium version of the mic, the <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Electro-Voice/635N-D">635N/D</a>.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Electro-Voice/635A">Electro-Voice 635A</a> is also known as: 635B, 635A/B, 635, 635A(B).</p>
